1: /**
2:  * BNJI.NET — public message board API boundary.
3:  *
4:  *   GET  /api/board                     newest-first visible messages (paginated)
5:  *        /api/board?limit=N              up to N messages (clamped to pageSize)
6:  *        /api/board?cursor=CURSOR        cursor-based pagination: returns the
7:  *                                       next page of older messages + a new cursor
8:  *   POST /api/board                     { text, image? } -> 201 { message }
9:  *
10:  * Cursor-based pagination: pass the nextCursor from one response to get the
11:  * next page. When nextCursor is absent, there are no more pages.
12:  *
13:  * This endpoint is NOT prerendered: it runs in the Worker on every request so
14:  * it can read environment bindings (storage) and enforce rate limits.
15:  *
16:  * Safety contract for user-generated content:
17:  *   - text: trimmed, control characters stripped, hard length cap; rendered
18:  *     client-side via textContent only (never innerHTML);
19:  *   - image: accepted ONLY as a data: URL of an allowed MIME type under the
20:  *     size cap; re-validated here (never trust the client); stored as-is and
21:  *     rendered in an <img> with no scripting surface;
22:  *   - rate limit: shared KV-based counter so different Worker isolates still
23:  *     throttle consistently; one post per cooldown per client address, plus
24:  *     an hourly cap;
25:  *   - moderation: hidden/deleted/reported messages never reach GET; status
26:  *     field exists for future moderation UI (schema + enforcement only);
27:  *   - no credentials ever flow to the client; storage secrets live in env.
28:  */
